WEBVTT

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:07.770
Damn it!

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.610
You were working with the Mongols?

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.360
Did they take your wives 
and children hostage?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.590
Tae...

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.500
My love...

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.460
Daddy!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.970
Sasamaru...

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.150
I just wanted...

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.500
He knew how to use a sword.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.810
And he had nerve.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.040
It's a shame to lose him.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.470
That forest!

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.330
Fire your arrows to smoke them out!

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.200
Tch! They're on the move.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.140
Princess!

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.770
Princess!

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.240
I'm fine...

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.520
Go.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.420
Get out of here, and get her patched up.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.000
Do not let that woman die!

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.930
Well, they're awake now.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.730
We're not close enough, 
and not far enough away, either.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.130
What do we do, Kuchii-dono?

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.780
Do we really attack?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.400
Or do we haul ass out of here?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.190
Haul ass?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.880
You still want to "haul 
ass" after you've seen this?

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.300
Hell...

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.080
Everyone, stay close!

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.100
Attack!

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.610
Don't let the Japanese into the camp!

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.290
Get the spearmen into formation!

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.100
Guess I don't have a choice...

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.130
Time to do this...

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.240
You... sons of bitches!

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.390
All right, I opened a hole into the camp, men!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.540
Whether yours is big or small, 
it's time to ram it in!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.120
Everyone, split up, but don't get lost!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.120
R-Reporting!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.270
We're under attack!

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.060
The northeast entrance to the camp!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:37.990
How many?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.680
Th-There were...

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.400
Five hundred?

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.800
N-No, one thousand?

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:48.110
You came to inform me without 
finding out how many there were?

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:52.100
Or, despite being commander of your zuun,

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.370
you simply wanted 
an excuse to flee the battle?

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:59.020
It seems you fear the Japanese soldiers 
more than you fear Kin Houkei.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.810
<b>Goryeo Army Commander (High Inspector) 
Kin Houkei</b>

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.270
Th-That's not true...

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:07.410
The darkness creates fear, and makes 
the enemy seem larger than he is.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.280
Listen to the sounds when 
you make your judgment.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.720
There aren't many.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.380
Sixty, seventy at most.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.470
<i>The way they're attacking at night, 
without fear of the overwhelming odds...</i>

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.290
<i>Perhaps it's the man who killed my son, 
the mingghan commander, this afternoon.</i>

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.940
<b>2nd Marshal in Command of the Mongol Armies 
(Eastern Expeditionary Force Vice Marshal of the Left) 
Ryuu Fukukou</b>

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.640
A duet between my matouqin 
and the screams of the battlefield.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.920
Is it to your liking?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.910
You're...

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.500
Ryuu Fukukou-sama...

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:54.110
<i>Vice Marshal of the 30,000-strong 
Mongol Eastern Expeditionary Force...</i>

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.210
You're a wise man to try to judge the 
enemy's size by the sound, Kin Houkei-dono.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.670
What's wrong?

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:10.250
What brings you to the Goryeo camp?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.420
Don't look so suspicious.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.570
I didn't tell the marshal I was coming.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:16.810
You're here in secret?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:22.320
I heard there's a wolf on this island, 
who slew a mingghan commander.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.010
<i>Damn Jurchen...</i>

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.490
<i>What are you planning?</i>

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.730
Okay, retreat!

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:34.060
We're getting out of here!

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.150
Already?

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.680
We just got here!

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.190
We showed them our fangs in this attack.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.970
But we can't stay long.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:44.530
If we stay too long, they'll invite us 
to stay for dinner and spend the night.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.540
Well, I don't want that.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.860
Did you hear something?

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:49.920
A scream?

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.610
It came from the shoreline.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.360
The beach!

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.400
There's lots of them on the beach!

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.750
The hostages they took from the Sasu Village?

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.210
They're planning on moving 
them to one of their big ships

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.860
to get them away from the night attack.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.550
General, let's go save them!

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.440
We can't abandon them!

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:09.440
No. If we get in any deeper, 
 we'll be surrounded.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.390
B-But if we go fast...

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.280
Tae... Sasamaru...

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.110
Get moving!

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.620
Do you want to get surrounded 
and slaughtered?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.580
Carefully! Carefully! Be careful!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.380
What... What happened to the attack?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.590
Did it work?

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:44.940
Well, Jinzaburou?

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.300
There's no time left.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.400
We need to leave!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.450
Damn it! Let's go, men.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.520
But...

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.780
The general says we abandon 
the women and children and run.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.810
What's that sound?

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:01.670
More enemies?

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.290
I don't know that flag!

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.490
Allies?

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.710
Who are they?

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:14.120
That flag... The Toibarai?

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.490
Toibarai?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.170
I once heard a story 
about descendants of people

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.090
who were originally sent 
to protect Japan from invaders...

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.330
They make their base in the mountains,

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.830
and don't follow the orders 
of the dazaifu or the local lord.

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:27.660
Stay strong, everyone.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.280
Show them the power of the Toibarai!

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.700
Looks like they're on our side.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.040
And they're quite strong.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:40.520
There's about 150 of them...

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.720
But this buys us a little time.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:43.760
Time?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:45.120
Okay, men.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:46.490
Yes, sir!

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.900
Run to the shore!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.430
Get moving!

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.170
No!

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:02.060
You okay?

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.200
My mother...

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.720
For now, we need to get out of here!

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.680
We need to get out of here 
before the Mongols calm down!

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.360
Is everybody keeping up?

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.240
Some of them are falling behind!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.940
Hey, come on!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.580
We won. Let's get out of here!

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.690
We'll serve as the rear guard!

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.390
Just don't stop! Run!

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.990
I didn't think our speedy night attack

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:28.930
would end with us 
carting off women and children.

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.710
But I think we can avoid a pursuit.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.190
Just maybe, yeah.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.180
<b>Toibarai Commander 
Nagamine Hangan</b>

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.810
Are you the warrior who uses Gikei-style?

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.770
Kuchii Jinzaburou.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:41.940
Who are you?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:44.660
Nagamine Hangan of the Toibarai.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.230
We're leaving.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.850
We have no desire to lose any more men 
for the sake of the local lord's troops.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.130
I see.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.380
You have my thanks.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.640
I guess I owe you 
"Toibarai" guys a favor, huh?

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.540
An uncouth way to say it, 
but I'm glad to hear you feel that way.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:01.840
Of course, this wasn't something 
we volunteered to do.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.540
A certain noble personage 
asked that we do this.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.840
If you are worthy, perhaps 
you'll see them someday.

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:15.500
Until then, wash that blood off of yourself.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.420
And wash your tongue, as well.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.690
Toibarai, we're retreating!

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.160
<i>Kuchii Jinzaburou.</i>

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.710
<i>I cannot imagine that you will 
be the one who brings us peace.</i>

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.050
<i>What does the emperor 
see in a man like that?</i>

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:47.280
There's no fun to be had in
cutting down these weeds!

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:53.810
I shall hunt the wolf we saw tonight.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.200
Are you the leader of the Japanese?

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.260
Who the hell are you?

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:07.490
No, you certainly don't comport 
yourself like a leader would.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.870
I don't know what the hell 
you're talking about,

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.200
but I do know one thing.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.800
You're pretty high up 
in the Mongol ranks, right?

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:19.310
But you don't seem 
to be a mere weed, either.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.410
I'll handle him.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.340
You are a worthy prey to hunt!

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:25.960
Wanna try it?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.310
You're quite strong!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:45.460
Excellent.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.770
You are truly worthy prey!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.600
What the hell are you talking about?

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.080
If this is some kind of sermon,
 then no thanks!

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:57.540
I am satisfied!

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.730
Weed!

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:07.140
Do not interfere with my hunt!

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.170
You're spoiling my fun!

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:16.810
You're not a weed, 
you're an impertinent, little fly!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:25.920
What?

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:34.370
I see...

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.260
It's you?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.640
You're tonight's wolf?

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:47.440
I'll strip off your skin and decorate 
the walls of my mansion with it!

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.940
Now... Come!

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.320
Come on, you slowpoke!

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:02.230
You asshole!

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.810
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:05.740
Wait! I won't let you get away!

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.220
Vice Marshal, you mustn't.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.440
That was an order from 
the marshal to return to base.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.980
Very well.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.860
It's hard to see the 
blood properly at night.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:25.210
I'll see him again,

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:28.880
and make the crimson blood 
pour from all his limbs!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.890
<b>Mongol Army Marshal (Eastern Expeditionary Force Marshal)  
Hindun</b>

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:47.530
Is Ryuu Fukukou back yet?

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:52.460
The vice marshal must have heard your order.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.520
He will return soon.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.910
He's a handful.

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.080
He has the required talent 
to be vice marshal,

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:04.980
but it seems he won't be satisfied 
unless he fights on the battlefield himself.

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:11.630
Come to think of it, I heard you fought 
a completely unnecessary one-on-one battle.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.920
I have nothing to say for myself, sir.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:21.530
It seems there's something on this island 
that changes even the coldest of generals.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:30.220
Priest, when does the great 
Tengri say we leave for Hakata?

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:34.970
Great Tengri has given me his words.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:41.440
October 13th is an auspicious day to set sail.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.320
Seven days, huh?

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:48.660
Until then, let us enjoy the banquet 
prepared for us here at Tsushima.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:54.920
May the great Khan and the great 
Mongol Empire reign for eternity!

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:56.580
May it reign for eternity!

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.780
Everyone here is really tough.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:17.690
I was worried we wouldn't be able to cross 
the mountains after that night attack.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:23.030
Thinking about going back to the capital 
is enough to make my exhaustion disappear.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:27.170
As of now, there's no sign 
we're being pursued.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.650
Did our night attack pay off?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.340
Hey, Shiraishi-dono.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:33.910
We're not ready to relax yet.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.700
I feel like I'm alive again!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.880
This is the perfect place 
for the people and horses to rest.

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:51.770
You finally came, huh?

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.510
Princess Teruhi...

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:08.330
I'm so glad you're safe, Princess!

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:11.480
I'm glad you're safe, as well.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.370
Even if the others aren't...

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.100
Really...

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:23.760
We can finally go home!

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.100
To the capital!

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:33.240
The Sasu Village women who came 
earlier have prepared some food.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.820
First, get some rest, everyone.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:38.390
Right!

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.360
Dantsuke mochi!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.140
This is great!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:47.260
You only ever get these at festivals.

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:55.130
This is strong bamboo.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:56.860
Sasara.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:57.600
Yes?

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.410
Get everyone's katanas.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:01.650
Our katanas?

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:06.280
Yeah. And bring anybody who's 
good at crafts or blacksmithing.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:08.760
I want something made, fast.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:13.720
This brings back memories, Gontarou.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.740
Of what, Kano?

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.670
When we were young, 
you stole one of these mochi

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:23.730
at Hachiman's festival, 
and I saw you get tied to a tree.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.180
Don't talk about it like it's a fun memory.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.370
<i>I'm glad...</i>

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.010
<i>Everyone's faces are still filled with life.</i>

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.600
How's your wound?

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.090
It's just a scratch!

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:48.120
Liar.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.720
How's she looking, Douen?

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.110
I gave her seven stitches or so.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.350
The bleeding stopped,
but she can't push herself.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:58.250
I see.

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.980
Hey, exile! You're being far too rude.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.180
You're chewing on mochi and—

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.900
This is sashimo grass.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.120
Sashimo grass?

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.250
My clan always uses this to heal wounds.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.290
How dare you!

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.390
We're almost to the capital.

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:20.070
Take it easy.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.090
I don't need you tell me that.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.220
<i>What was that about?</i>

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.460
Gisuke, how are you doing?

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:37.410
I'm fine...

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:40.260
My clan uses this sashimo grass...

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:45.760
<i>He's cheering up the injured, huh?</i>

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.740
<i>I passed under a blade...</i>

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.400
<i>So that's why...</i>

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:55.790
Oh...

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:59.740
Who said you could eat that, brat?!

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.540
Jinta, stop it.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:02.830
It's not the kid's fault.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.310
I'm not going to stop!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.790
He's the child of a filthy traitor!

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:09.420
Don't insult my dad...

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:10.790
What did you say?

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:12.800
What's going on?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.530
That's Sasamaru.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.030
He's Ginshichi's child.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:21.200
Ginshichi's child?

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.880
He was with the hostages we saved.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:25.900
But we haven't found the mother...

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:31.430
Your father betrayed the rest of us 
from the village who joined the attack!

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:34.740
My child was kidnapped by 
the Mongols and isn't coming back!

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:38.470
So why is his brat still here?

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:40.740
Boss...

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:48.500
The man who killed my father...

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.590
What's wrong?

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:52.540
Look up and glare at me.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.170
I killed your dad.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.190
My father's katana.

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.170
Now use this to take revenge.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.650
What's wrong?

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:21.720
You can't do it?

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.560
You're not like him...

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:27.280
Your father was a brave man.

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:29.790
Brave?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.870
That's right.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.170
He challenged someone far stronger than he

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:36.330
to save his wife and child.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.850
Sasamaru, you need to become strong, too,

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.700
and avenge your father!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.480
Fine.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:53.390
I'll become strong, 
and someday, I'll kill you.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.070
I'll be right there, waiting for you.

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.550
Let's head off...

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:11.040
<b>Episode 4: 
Back to the Capital</b>

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.810
Back to the capital.

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:48.080
Oh, we're all the way 
to the great Keyaki tree already.

00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:50.890
People of Sasu, once we're to its base,

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:53.820
we'll be right near the capital...

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:58.150
<i>I'm sure the mansion will be quiet,
 even after I get back...</i>

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:07.100
What's wrong?

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.060
<i>The capital...</i>

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:33.370
<i>is burning...</i>

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:36.300
<i>It's all burning...</i>
